<title>FRANCE: France records 26th mad cow case.</title>
<headline>France records 26th mad cow case.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France has registered its 26th case of mad cow disease the Agriculture Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The herd of 42 animals, in the western region of Britanny, was slaughtered on Monday, it said.</p>
<p>The mad cow crisis came to a head last year when the European Commission imposed a worldwide ban on beef exports from Britain, the country worst hit by the Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy (BSE).</p>
